  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_019, acc=0.639) uses pca_n2000 as the RNA encoder in a multimodal, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted-fusion setup. RNA is clearly the dominant signal (RNA-only multiprofile+avgpool=0.591 vs image-only=0.208), and the multimodal gain over RNA-only is modest (~5%), suggesting the RNA representation quality is the primary bottleneck. We have zero data on how learned RNA encoders (scvi_n200, scgpt) compare to PCA. Question tested: Does replacing pca_n2000 with scvi_n200 in the best-performing multimodal configuration improve validation accuracy, i.e., does a learned generative latent representation outperform a linear PCA projection for downstream classification? Why best next experiment: config_031 is a clean single-variable swap (RNA encoder only) against the current champion config_019, making the result directly interpretable. It targets the highest-impact unexplored design axis (RNA encoder) while holding all other settings at their empirically validated best values (multiprofile, avgpool, resnet50, weighted fusion), maximizing information gained per experiment under the limited budget."
}

